#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
eve-netboot -- the EVE Netboot Installer VM appliance
=====================================================

One command for everything the appliance does:

  eve-netboot boot           run at every boot (eve-netboot-setup.service):
                             grow the disk, apply settings passed in through
                             cloud-init, start the stack
  eve-netboot console        the screen on tty1 (eve-netboot-console.service):
                             setup wizard until the appliance is set up, then
                             a status screen with a login to the menu
  eve-netboot menu           the settings menu (admin, after login)
  eve-netboot status         status as text
  eve-netboot apply          apply /etc/eve-netboot/settings.env
  eve-netboot logs [svc]     follow the logs of the stack
  eve-netboot sync           check GitHub for new EVE-OS releases now
  eve-netboot update-system  Debian updates (apt), with a check afterwards
  eve-netboot update-app     newest EVE Netboot Installer release, with rollback
  eve-netboot export         print the settings as KEY=VALUE text
  eve-netboot web            the HTTPS management UI (eve-netboot-web.service)

Settings live in /etc/eve-netboot/settings.env (KEY=VALUE). Settings passed in
through cloud-init (plain KEY=VALUE user-data, or an "eve_netboot:" mapping in
a #cloud-config) are merged into that file whenever the user-data changes.
"""

